rates over 48 h in the Cell-IQ ® …\n\n**FIGURE 4**\n\nDiagram of individual colony proliferation rates over 48 h in the Cell-IQ®. Progenitor colonies (cell numbers beyond 32) are indicated in bold. The dashed lines represent the threshold of the minimum cell number considered to be a progenitor colony (n = 32). PAvas: progenitor avascular meniscal cells, PVas: progenitor vascular meniscal cells, PChs: chondroprogenitors.\n\n [![FIGURE 5](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/5163abd90bd3/fbioe-10-1003966-g005.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/808b5f752953/fbioe-10-1003966-g005.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFIGURE 5\n\n**\n\nThe comparison of colony proliferation…\n\n**\n\nFIGURE 5\n\n**\n\nThe comparison of colony proliferation rate (colony cell >32 cells) for avascular (PAvas)…\n\n**FIGURE 5**\n\nThe comparison of colony proliferation rate (colony cell >32 cells) for avascular (PAvas) (n = 7), vascular meniscal progenitors (PVas) (n = 7) and chondroprogenitors (PChs) (n = 6). Date showed the mean cell number of progenitor colonies in every 6 h.\n\n [![FIGURE 6](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/f7b1692f86fb/fbioe-10-1003966-g006.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/0c792fae4868/fbioe-10-1003966-g006.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFIGURE 6\n\n**\n\nMeniscus and cartilage derived mixed…\n\n**\n\nFIGURE 6\n\n**\n\nMeniscus and cartilage derived mixed cell and progenitor immunoprofiles; Histograms showing the percentage…\n\n**FIGURE 6**\n\nMeniscus and cartilage derived mixed cell and progenitor immunoprofiles; Histograms showing the percentage of cells with immunopositivity for cell surface markers on donor matched mixed or progenitor avascular and vascular meniscal cells and chondrocytes at passage 2–3. Data were presented as mean ± standard deviation (n = 5).\n\n [![FIGURE 7](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/246dfe0d87c0/fbioe-10-1003966-g007.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/4d34670e3f58/fbioe-10-1003966-g007.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFIGURE 7\n\n**\n\nGAG/DNA quantitation after 28 days…\n\n**\n\nFIGURE 7\n\n**\n\nGAG/DNA quantitation after 28 days of 3D pellet culture. Comparison of mixed populations…\n\n**FIGURE 7**\n\nGAG/DNA quantitation after 28 days of 3D pellet culture. Comparison of mixed populations and progenitor (pro) avascular and vascular meniscal cells and chondrocytes from five donor matched samples. Data were presented as mean ± standard deviation (n = 3 pellets/donor).\n\n [![FIGURE 8](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/be15a0411bb1/fbioe-10-1003966-g008.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/94af53e8e1f0/fbioe-10-1003966-g008.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFIGURE 8\n\n**\n\nChondrogenesis of both mixed population…\n\n**\n\nFIGURE 8\n\n**\n\nChondrogenesis of both mixed population and progenitor cells from avascular and vascular meniscus…\n\n**FIGURE 8**\n\nChondrogenesis of both mixed population and progenitor cells from avascular and vascular meniscus and cartilage from a representative patient 5, assessed by staining sections using type I and type II collagen immunohistochemistry and toluidine blue metachromatic staining of GAGs. Calibration bars = 250 μm. Avas: Avascular meniscal cells; Vas: Vascular meniscal cells; Chs: Chondrocytes.\n\n [![FIGURE 9](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/d12ffb491de5/fbioe-10-1003966-g009.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/00f5/9629835/43e73dffa191/fbioe-10-1003966-g009.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFIGURE 9\n\n**\n\nSemi-quantitative immunohistochemical staining measurement for…\n\n**\n\nFIGURE 9\n\n**\n\nSemi-quantitative immunohistochemical staining measurement for collagen type I **(A)** and collagen type II **…**\n\n**FIGURE 9**\n\nSemi-quantitative immunohistochemical staining measurement for collagen type I **(A)** and collagen type II **(B)** of mixed population (MAvas, MVas, MChs) and progenitor (PAvas, PVas, PChs) avascular and vascular meniscal cells and chondrocytes pellets. Data were presented as mean ± standard deviation.\n\nAll figures (9)\n\n[See this image and copyright information in PMC](#)\n\n## References\n\n1.  1.  Benya P. (1982). Dedifferentiated chondrocytes reexpress the differentiated collagen phenotype when cultured in agarose gels. Cell 30, 215–224. 10.1016/0092-8674(82)90027-7 - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/0092-8674\\(82\\)90027-7) - [PubMed](/7127471/)\n2.  1.  Brinkhof B., Zhang B., Cui Z., Ye H., Wang H. (2020). ALCAM (CD166) as a gene expression marker for human mesenchymal stromal cell characterisation. Gene 763, 100031. 10.1016/j.gene.2020.100031 - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.gene.2020.100031) - [PubMed](/34493362/)\n3.  1.  Buckley C. D., Filer A. (2017). “Fibroblasts and fibroblast-like synoviocytes,” in Kelley and firestein’s textbook of rheumatology (Elsevier; ), 231–249. e4. 10.1016/B978-0-323-31696-5.00014-0 - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-323-31696-5.00014-0)\n4.  1.  Bush P. G., Hall A. C. (2003). The volume and morphology of chondrocytes within non-degenerate and degenerate human articular cartilage. Osteoarthr. Cartil. 11, 242–251. 10.1016/S1063-4584(02)00369-2 - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/s1063-4584\\(02\\)00369-2) - [PubMed](/12681950/)\n5.  1.  Chahla J., Papalamprou A., Chan V., Arabi Y., Salehi K., Nelson T. J., et al. (2021). Assessing the resident progenitor cell population and the vascularity of the adult human meniscus. Arthrosc. J. Arthrosc. Relat. Surg. 37, 252–265. 10.1016/j.arthro.2020.09.021 - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arthro.2020.09.021) - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7829352/) - [PubMed](/32979500/)\n\nShow all 40 references\n\n## Grants and funding\n\n-   [18480/VAC\\_/Versus Arthritis/United Kingdom](/?term=18480%2FVAC_%2FVersus+Arthritis%2FUnited+Kingdom%5BGrants+and+Funding%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc \"All articles for grant 18480/VAC_/Versus Arthritis/United Kingdom\")\n-   [20253/VAC\\_/Versus Arthritis/United Kingdom]