{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778978020044,"sessionID":"ses_1cca63944ffeC0p4p9EyTjkYHl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_OOmcVHySSiVfe7iB7mJT0hAI","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":35320,"limit":30},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n35320: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4072103 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000134 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002073)))\n35321: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072103 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0042634))\n35322: \n35323: # Class: obo:CL_4072104 (fibrochondrocyte)\n35324: \n35325: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28939894\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34608249\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072104 \"A chondrocyte with hybrid fibroblastic-chondrogenic characteristics found in fibrocartilage, particularly in the avascular inner zone and transitional middle zone of the meniscus. In humans, fibrochondrocytes are marked by predominant expression of type I collagen (COL1A1) and fibril-associated collagens (COL3A1, COL6A1), while retaining type II collagen (COL2A1) expression and exhibiting lower SOX9 than hyaline chondrocytes. This molecular profile underlies the synthesis of abundant type I collagen essential for fibrocartilage matrix and reflects an intermediate phenotype between fibroblast and chondrocyte.\")\n35326: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4072104 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35327: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34608249\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4072104 \"fibrocartilage chondrocyte\")\n35328: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28939894\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_4072104 \"meniscus fibrochondrocyte\")\n35329: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072104 \"FC\")\n35330: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072104 \"fibrochondrocyte\")\n35331: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000138 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001995)))\n35332: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 obo:CL_0002320)\n35333: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\n35334: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003328))\n35335: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003353))\n35336: \n35337: # Class: obo:CL_7770002 (juxtacanalicular tissue cell)\n35338: \n35339: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25356439\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39829808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770002 \"A trabecular meshwork cell of the juxtacanalicular tissue (JCT), characterized by a spindle-shaped, fibroblast-like morphology within a loose extracellular matrix immediately adjacent to Schlemm's canal. It expresses CHI3L1 (human and mouse) and ANGPTL7 (human), as well as smooth muscle actin for contractility. Unlike other trabecular meshwork cells, it does not form monolayers but exists in a loose network, regulating aqueous humor outflow resistance through continuous ECM remodelling, mechanotransduction, and formation of intracellular pores historically called giant vacuoles.\")\n35340: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_7770002 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3275\")\n35341: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_7770002 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35342: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_7770002 \"2025-01-29T08:52:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35343: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_7770002 \"JCT cell\")\n35344: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_7770002 \"juxtacanalicular tissue cell\")\n35345: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 obo:CL_0000327)\n35346: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 obo:CL_0002367)\n35347: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070278))\n35348: \n35349: # Class: obo:CL_7770003 (beam A cell)\n\n(Showing lines 35320-35349 of 35467. Use offset=35350 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4072103 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000134 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002073)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072103 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0042634))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4072104 (fibrochondrocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28939894\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34608249\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072104 \"A chondrocyte with hybrid fibroblastic-chondrogenic characteristics found in fibrocartilage, particularly in the avascular inner zone and transitional middle zone of the meniscus. In humans, fibrochondrocytes are marked by predominant expression of type I collagen (COL1A1) and fibril-associated collagens (COL3A1, COL6A1), while retaining type II collagen (COL2A1) expression and exhibiting lower SOX9 than hyaline chondrocytes. This molecular profile underlies the synthesis of abundant type I collagen essential for fibrocartilage matrix and reflects an intermediate phenotype between fibroblast and chondrocyte.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4072104 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34608249\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4072104 \"fibrocartilage chondrocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28939894\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_4072104 \"meniscus fibrochondrocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072104 \"FC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072104 \"fibrochondrocyte\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000138 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001995)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 obo:CL_0002320)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003328))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003353))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_7770002 (juxtacanalicular tissue cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25356439\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39829808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770002 \"A trabecular meshwork cell of the juxtacanalicular tissue (JCT), characterized by a spindle-shaped, fibroblast-like morphology within a loose extracellular matrix immediately adjacent to Schlemm's canal. It expresses CHI3L1 (human and mouse) and ANGPTL7 (human), as well as smooth muscle actin for contractility. Unlike other trabecular meshwork cells, it does not form monolayers but exists in a loose network, regulating aqueous humor outflow resistance through continuous ECM remodelling, mechanotransduction, and formation of intracellular pores historically called giant vacuoles.\")","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778978019927,"end":1778978020042}},"id":"prt_e335a5a42001KiuN5wi63BpMlU","sessionID":"ses_1cca63944ffeC0p4p9EyTjkYHl","messageID":"msg_e335a39a6001U6MLb66BjsNv8H"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778978020120,"sessionID":"ses_1cca63944ffeC0p4p9EyTjkYHl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_kEgNGE08dH5t2vDPeoCYZ4p6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":25592,"limit":24},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n25592: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020017 \"naive macrophage\")\n25593: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020017 \"non-activated macrophage\")\n25594: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1186/s12885-022-09872-y\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020017 \"resting-state macrophages\")\n25595: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020017 \"M0 macrophage\")\n25596: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020017 obo:CL_0000235)\n25597: \n25598: # Class: obo:CL_0020018 (proliferative fibrochondrocyte)\n25599: \n25600: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39759119\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020018 \"A fibrochondrocyte located in fibrocartilage that exhibits active proliferation capacity and is in S phase of the cell cycle. It functions as a progenitor cell positioned at the root of developmental trajectories alongside fibrochondrocyte progenitors (FCP), with the capacity to diverge toward one of two developmental fates: (1) fibrochondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes, or (2) regulatory chondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes. It is characterised by co-expression of COL1A1, the growth factors FGF7 and CTGF, and the cell-cycle genes STMN1, KIAA0101, and MCM3 in humans. During early progenitor differentiation, FGF7 and COL1A1 expression increases and then declines as the cell commits to terminal fates.\")\n25601: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020018 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n25602: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020018 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n25603: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020018 \"2025-11-27T12:48:39Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n25604: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020018 \"ProFC\")\n25605: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020018 \"Lineage relationships are inferred from single-cell RNA-seq trajectories and validated through experimental approaches, including FACS isolation, functional differentiation assays, and in vivo developmental gene expression analysis.\")\n25606: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020018 \"proliferative fibrochondrocyte\")\n25607: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 obo:CL_4072104)\n25608: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000056 obo:GO_0022402))\n25609: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\n25610: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000007498))\n25611: \n25612: # Class: obo:CL_0020019 (regulatory chondrocyte)\n25613: \n25614: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30026257\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34045450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37660146\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020019 \"A chondrocyte located mainly in the superficial zone of articular cartilage. In healthy human cartilage, regulatory chondrocytes are characterized by expression of EIF5A, PGK1, ANXA1, and TUBA1A. During osteoarthritis, a distinct subpopulation expands, marked by high expression of CHI3L1, CHI3L2, CRTAC1, and AEBP1, with enrichment for signaling pathway regulation (including Toll-like receptor, mTOR, and TGF-beta signaling) and antigen-processing gene expression, with a small proportion expressing MHC class II genes, suggesting potential immune cell-like regulatory functions during osteoarthritis progression.\")\n25615: AnnotationAssertion(dc:creator obo:CL_0020019 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n\n(Showing lines 25592-25615 of 35467. Use offset=25616 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020017 \"naive macrophage\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020017 \"non-activated macrophage\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1186/s12885-022-09872-y\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020017 \"resting-state macrophages\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020017 \"M0 macrophage\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020017 obo:CL_0000235)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020018 (proliferative fibrochondrocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39759119\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020018 \"A fibrochondrocyte located in fibrocartilage that exhibits active proliferation capacity and is in S phase of the cell cycle. It functions as a progenitor cell positioned at the root of developmental trajectories alongside fibrochondrocyte progenitors (FCP), with the capacity to diverge toward one of two developmental fates: (1) fibrochondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes, or (2) regulatory chondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes. It is characterised by co-expression of COL1A1, the growth factors FGF7 and CTGF, and the cell-cycle genes STMN1, KIAA0101, and MCM3 in humans. During early progenitor differentiation, FGF7 and COL1A1 expression increases and then declines as the cell commits to terminal fates.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020018 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020018 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020018 \"2025-11-27T12:48:39Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020018 \"ProFC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020018 \"Lineage relationships are inferred from single-cell RNA-seq trajectories and validated through experimental approaches, including FACS isolation, functional differentiation assays, and in vivo developmental gene expression analysis.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020018 \"proliferative fibrochondrocyte\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 obo:CL_4072104)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000056 obo:GO_0022402))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000007498))\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778978020028,"end":1778978020118}},"id":"prt_e335a5a9f0014237Mj7FMh3tcP","sessionID":"ses_1cca63944ffeC0p4p9EyTjkYHl","messageID":"msg_e335a39a6001U6MLb66BjsNv8H"}}
