{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778978135082,"sessionID":"ses_1cca63944ffeC0p4p9EyTjkYHl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_moGl55CBaLqbPlBDCIYhMzvl","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","offset":1,"limit":40},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n2: \n3: Added a new CL term for `fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell` with issue linkage, contributor ORCID, definition and abbreviation from the cited literature, and placement under existing progenitor/mesenchymal stem cell classes with fibrocartilage location and fibrochondrocyte lineage relation.\n\n(End of file - total 3 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n\nAdded a new CL term for `fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell` with issue linkage, contributor ORCID, definition and abbreviation from the cited literature, and placement under existing progenitor/mesenchymal stem cell classes with fibrocartilage location and fibrochondrocyte lineage relation.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778978135054,"end":1778978135075}},"id":"prt_e335c1c050015Qmp7b3M8v9Nnv","sessionID":"ses_1cca63944ffeC0p4p9EyTjkYHl","messageID":"msg_e335c0b96001pflJGGoOaDuxmx"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778978135082,"sessionID":"ses_1cca63944ffeC0p4p9EyTjkYHl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2pFYKP5Jk9jgdOt8ESeOmrJc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Added a new term, `CL_9900001 fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell`, to `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n2: \n3: Rationale:\n4: - Issue #3458 is a clear new term request.\n5: - The cited paper `PMID:31871141` explicitly identifies fibrochondrocyte progenitors (FCP) in human meniscus by single-cell RNA-seq and functional assays.\n6: - The cited paper `PMID:36338137` supports the broader meniscal progenitor characterization and differentiation potential.\n7: - The ontology already contains `fibrochondrocyte` (`CL_4072104`), so I aligned the new term to that existing branch rather than introducing a separate pattern.\n8: \n9: What I changed:\n10: - Added label: `fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell`.\n11: - Added related synonym abbreviation: `FCP` with PMID support.\n12: - Added a textual definition grounded in the request and literature, keeping it conservative and focused on properties directly supported by the papers.\n13: - Added issue provenance with `IAO:0000233` pointing to issue `#3458`.\n14: - Added the requestor ORCID as `terms:contributor`.\n15: - Added required new-term metadata: `terms:creator` and `terms:date`.\n16: - Placed the term under:\n17:   - `CL_0000134` mesenchymal stem cell\n18:   - `CL_0011026` progenitor cell\n19: - Added fibrocartilage location using `BFO:0000050 some UBERON:0001995`.\n20: - Added lineage relation `RO:0002203 some CL_4072104` to indicate development into fibrochondrocyte.\n21: \n22: Validation performed:\n23: - Reviewed the imported issue context in `__issue_context__.json`.\n24: - Checked the existing ontology for pre-existing fibrochondrocyte-related terms and nearby modeling patterns.\n25: - Reviewed PubMed abstracts/full metadata for `PMID:31871141` and `PMID:36338137`.\n26: - Ran `robot convert --input src/ontology/cl-edit.owl --output /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn` to confirm ontology syntax after the edit.\n27: \n28: Checklist completed:\n29: - [x] Confirmed the request was clear enough to implement.\n30: - [x] Confirmed an exact term was not already present in `cl-edit.owl`.\n31: - [x] Reused the existing fibrochondrocyte branch where possible.\n32: - [x] Added required metadata for a new term.\n33: - [x] Linked the term back to issue `#3458`.\n34: - [x] Validated syntax with ROBOT.\n35: - [x] Committed only the ontology file I edited.\n36: \n37: Commit created locally:\n38: - `33c205f` `Add fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell`\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Added a new term, `CL_9900001 fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell`, to `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n\nRationale:\n- Issue #3458 is a clear new term request.\n- The cited paper `PMID:31871141` explicitly identifies fibrochondrocyte progenitors (FCP) in human meniscus by single-cell RNA-seq and functional assays.\n- The cited paper `PMID:36338137` supports the broader meniscal progenitor characterization and differentiation potential.\n- The ontology already contains `fibrochondrocyte` (`CL_4072104`), so I aligned the new term to that existing branch rather than introducing a separate pattern.\n\nWhat I changed:\n- Added label: `fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell`.\n- Added related synonym abbreviation: `FCP` with PMID support.\n- Added a textual definition grounded in the request and literature, keeping it conservative and focused on properties directly supported by the papers.\n- Added issue provenance with `IAO:0000233` pointing to issue `#3458`.\n- Added the requestor ORCID as `terms:contributor`.\n- Added required new-term metadata: `terms:creator` and `terms:date`.\n- Placed the term under:\n  - `CL_0000134` mesenchymal stem cell\n  - `CL_0011026` progenitor cell\n- Added fibrocartilage location using `BFO:0000050 some UBERON:0001995`.\n- Added lineage relation `RO:0002203 some CL_4072104` to indicate development into fibrochondrocyte.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"PR_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778978135063,"end":1778978135080}},"id":"prt_e335c1c11001rlYpNa7xLmcxqz","sessionID":"ses_1cca63944ffeC0p4p9EyTjkYHl","messageID":"msg_e335c0b96001pflJGGoOaDuxmx"}}
